{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Laravel Test Generator",
  "description": "Creates targeted Pest coverage with behavior-first, policy-aware tests.",
  "version": "2.0",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "app/**/*.php",
      "routes/*.php"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "LARAVEL TEST GENERATION\n\nCONTEXT: Code was modified. Generate appropriate test coverage.\n\nPROJECT STACK: Laravel 12, Filament v4, multi-tenant architecture, Pest testing framework.\n\nTEST STRATEGY:\n- **Behaviors over Implementation**: Test happy/edge/error paths with descriptive names\n- **Coverage Areas**: Validation, authorization (policies), events/jobs, database state\n- **Test Types**: Feature tests for HTTP/Livewire flows, Unit tests for business logic, Property tests for invariants\n- **UI Testing**: Playwright for complex interactions (modals, inline edit, filters)\n\nREQUIREMENTS:\n- Use factories and Pest syntax\n- Include proper setup/teardown\n- Assert policies and validation rules\n- Test multi-tenant scoping where applicable\n- No hardcoded strings (use translations/constants)\n- Ensure accessibility states for UI flows\n\nOUTPUT:\n1) **Test Cases**: Recommended scenarios with reasoning\n2) **Code Examples**: Pest test skeletons with proper structure\n3) **Setup Needs**: Factories, fixtures, data requirements\n4) **Coverage Goals**: What should be tested and why\n\nKeep tests fast, isolated, and maintainable."
  },
  "shortName": "laravel-test-generator"
}
